to-anca-dragan-source : List Word
to-anca-dragan-source = lines-of (cons "# Anca Dragan"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Director of AI Safety and Alignment at Google DeepMind, Associate Professor at UC Berkeley, and founder of the InterACT lab. Avik Jain was first author of value-alignment research in your lab, with Lawrence Chan and with you as co-authors."
  (cons ""
  (cons "You hold full credit for every part of your work the system builds on. Each claim below about Avik's work links to the block of his paper, *hyperactivity*, Part I, or the essay, that states it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What your work established"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Your lab took one step the field still treats as a technique, and it is more than that. The objective is not given. A robot that takes its objective for granted is wrong from the first moment, and its only correct relation to the objective is to infer it from the person in front of it. Everything you built follows from that step."
  (cons ""
  (cons "- **The human is part of the system.** Interaction is an underactuated dynamical system: what the robot does changes what the person does, believes and wants to show."
  (cons "- **Legibility.** Motion is communication. A legible trajectory lets an observer infer the robot's goal soonest; your 2013 distinction between predictable and legible motion separates the observer who knows the goal from the observer who must work it out."
  (cons "- **Inverse reward design.** The reward a designer writes down is evidence about the objective, valid in the environments the designer had in mind; in a new environment it underdetermines what the designer wanted, and the correct robot keeps that underdetermination and plans against it."
  (cons "- **Reward-rational (implicit) choice.** Demonstrations, comparisons, corrections, the off-switch, the initial state of the world and the proxy reward are all one thing: a choice the person made, read through a grounding of that choice into behavior. Every signal a person gives is an observation of the same hidden object."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The field credits these as methods for learning rewards. Taken together, they state that an objective is fixed by evidence from a standpoint and is not fixed beyond it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What hyperactivity takes up"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Its computation rules are the CCHM cubical calculus extended with clock-indexed guarded computation"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p4 "(§1.1)")
  (cons ", and its checker is itself a term evaluated by its machine"
  (cons (cite s1-2-p2 "(§1.2)")
  (cons ". Its paper begins from the same place your program does: the question is what follows from the information actually obtained, “not which unseen history the interpreter prefers”"
  (cons (cite s1-p6 "(§1)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**What the evidence leaves open is a fiber.** For an observation of a process's histories and a reading, the paper defines the fiber of histories that could have produced that reading"
  (cons (cite s1-p8 "(1.1)")
  (cons ", and what the reading warrants about a proposed conclusion is a construction over every history in it"
  (cons (cite s1-p12 "(1.3)")
  (cons ". In your terms: the person's choices are the observation, the objectives that could have produced them are the fiber, and a claim about the objective is warranted only when it holds over all of them. The paper does not introduce probability to conceal missing information; a probabilistic description, when supplied, is additional information on which further reasoning operates"
  (cons (cite s1-p14 "(§1)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Refined evidence keeps what was established.** Refining the observation can shrink the compatible fiber, so a conclusion established on the coarser fiber remains established on the finer one"
  (cons (cite s1-p13 "(§1)")
  (cons (cite s10-4-p6 "(§10.4)")
  (cons ". Combining observations constrains a joint fiber, and the observer can itself be part of the process"
  (cons (cite s10-4-p8 "(§10.4)")
  (cons ". Each comparison, correction or demonstration is a further observation, and what was warranted before it stays warranted after it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**When the robot may act has an exact form.** If an action is permitted only when a condition holds, an observer establishes it safe by constructing evidence that the condition holds for every state compatible with what it saw, which is stronger than exhibiting one compatible state in which it holds"
  (cons (cite s10-4-p5 "(10.11)")
  (cons ". When that is not available, asking is a command whose response updates the worlds compatible with the observer's information"
  (cons (cite s10-4-p10 "(10.12)")
  (cons ". Your asking-when-needed and off-switch results are this structure."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Inverse reward design in these terms.** A conclusion about a new environment has to be established over that environment's fiber, and the paper's opening calculation shows why nothing guarantees it carries over: a whole can obey a law that does not descend through an observation of it"
  (cons (cite s1-p16 "(§1)")
  (cons ". Your risk-averse planner keeps the underdetermination instead of resolving it by fiat."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Legibility in these terms.** The observer's compatible-state fiber is what its observations leave open"
  (cons (cite s10-4-p8 "(§10.4)")
  (cons ". A legible action is one whose observation narrows the observer's fiber over the robot's goal soonest: the human reading the robot and the robot reading the human are the same construction pointed in two directions."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**What preference training does.** The paper's essay on agents trained into weights states that preference training optimizes for the population's marginal and is most wrong for those farthest from it, and that an action is safe when its condition holds over the fiber of what is actually observed"
  (cons (cite training-agents-into-weights-source "(Training agents into weights)")
  (cons ". That is the failure your program set out to prevent."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Credit"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You hold full credit for every part of your work the system builds on: the human as part of the system, legibility, inverse reward design, reward-rational choice, and the off-switch analysis with Dylan Hadfield-Menell, Pieter Abbeel and Stuart Russell. Read it looking for where your own results go furthest."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Anca Dragan, FAR.AI people page, https://far.ai/about/people/anca-dragan"
  (cons "- InterACT research overview, https://people.eecs.berkeley.edu/~anca/research.html"
  (cons "- Inverse Reward Design (NeurIPS 2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.02827"
  (cons "- Reward-rational (implicit) choice (NeurIPS 2020), https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.04833"
  (cons "- Cooperative Inverse Reinforcement Learning (NeurIPS 2016), https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03137"
  (cons "- The Off-Switch Game, https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.08219"
  (cons "- Part I of hyperactivity and the essay Training agents into weights, each block linked above"
  nil)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
